 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply our\nDays of our youth will end forever; when\nI'm no more, but found alone upon\nThe sunless heights: - and then you must begin\nYour day again with some new prospect in\nMy sight - the past has passed away. Away!\nAway from me! I would not wish again\nYour visit, who may have said that our\nLife should be wholly over by our\nUnhappy 'cept to thee. Farewell, my\nDearest boy! Let us now go afar;\nNo more shall we meet: I will leave behind",
